        "subject": "LU-20948 o2iblnd: renew a FastReg MR after a failed tx",
        "message": "LU-20948 o2iblnd: renew a FastReg MR after a failed tx\n\no2iblnd posts LOCAL_INV and REG_MR before a FastReg RDMA. It bumps\nthe MR key when it maps the descriptor. A QP flush can drop both work\nrequests, so the HCA keeps the old key. The next LOCAL_INV on that\ndescriptor then fails, and the QP goes to error. Each conn that gets\nthe descriptor fails the same way, until o2iblnd frees the idle pool.\n\nA tx can fail after o2iblnd posts its LOCAL_INV and REG_MR. Then\nkiblnd_fmr_pool_unmap() gives the descriptor a new MR, or frees the\ndescriptor if the allocation fails. A simulated send error posts\nnothing, so the descriptor keeps its LOCAL_INV for the next post.\n\n    Soft-RoCE, 2 VMs, lst brw 1M read and write, 5 s RoCE drop\n    during load, 6 cycles\n    without the fix: bulk 0 MiB/s after cycle 1, 43 LOCAL_INV\n                     failures in rxe_invalidate_mr()\n    with the fix:    bulk 14-30 MiB/s in each cycle, no LOCAL_INV\n                     failures, 29 MR renewals\n\nFixes: f2600449ced3 (\"LU-5783 o2iblnd: Add Fast Reg memory registration support\")\nFixes: 0c93919f1375 (\"LU-16349 o2iblnd: Fix key mismatch issue\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: I3f2952d8f98fa09c4b5cc9e9f74ac75a5c4e0e40\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
